1. Uniform Orchestration Mode

All VM instances are identical and managed as a single group.

Characteristics
Same VM size
Same OS image
Same configuration
Azure manages instance placement and scaling
Best for stateless applications
Use Cases
Web applications
API servers
Microservices
Application servers behind a Load Balancer
2. Flexible Orchestration Mode

VMs can have different configurations within the same scale set.

Characteristics
Different VM sizes allowed
Different OS images allowed
Supports standalone VMs and availability zones
More control over individual VMs
Suitable for stateful workloads
Use Cases
Database clusters
Domain Controllers
Enterprise applications
Mixed workload environments

